{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779313438,"nonce":"f+hp3s/zxQXOktNW8KdOwj4dvio=","title":"Studio: support dynamic Mux ports for task data concatenation","message":"Support a visually clean dynamic Mux/concatenation component for combining named task-data signals into a single model input vector.\n\nContext:\n- Feedbax already has a Mux component and Studio registry entry for concatenating inputs.\n- Delayed-reach task data should eventually expose separate signals such as target position and cues, which then need to be combined before network.input.\n- The desired UX starts with two mux input ports, adds another input when the existing exposed ports are wired and the user drags another connection in, and shrinks back when trailing extra ports are unwired.\n\nDecisions:\n- Dynamic mux ports are model graph structure, not task data.\n- The dynamic behavior should be deterministic and schema-backed so validation and lowering agree on generated in_N ports.\n- Keep at least two input ports visible by default.\n- Additional ports should appear only as needed and should collapse when no longer used, without leaving stale binding records.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Mux nodes render with at least in_0 and in_1.\n- Dragging a third/fourth input into a fully occupied mux creates the next input port in a stable way.\n- Unwiring trailing dynamic ports shrinks the visible mux back down to the minimum viable port count.\n- Validation/schema projection knows about generated mux input ports.\n- The UI remains readable and avoids jumpy layout when ports expand or shrink.\n- Tests cover generated port projection and cleanup.","files":null}]}